News and public source catalog
------------------------------
News feed choices reference World Monitor (https://github.com/koala73/worldmonitor),
including src/config/feeds.ts and server/worldmonitor/news/v1/_feeds.ts.
No World Monitor implementation code is incorporated.

News titles, source summaries, article excerpts, full readable source
content and images remain attributable to their original publishers.
The application retains source links and distinguishes source content
from Agent-generated summaries. The code license grants no rights to
third-party news content. Material in demonstration screenshots retains
the original source attribution visible in the application.

Weather and other signal sources
--------------------------------
Forecasts use Open-Meteo (https://open-meteo.com/), with data under CC BY 4.0;
the free API service has separate non-commercial usage conditions.
The application retains forecast source and retrieval metadata.

Calendar data references NateScarlet/holiday-cn
(https://github.com/NateScarlet/holiday-cn), Copyright (c) 2019 NateScarlet,
under the MIT License (see LICENSES/NateScarlet-holiday-cn-MIT.txt).
Exchange-rate data references fawazahmed0/exchange-api
(https://github.com/fawazahmed0/exchange-api); it is not central bank data.
Calendar and exchange-rate modules are retained as source dependencies;
no development fixtures or user runtime records are included in the ZIP.
